From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: k230: keep the gate on mux changes and do not reparent

k230_clk_composite_set_parent() writes only the new mux field to the mux
register. On clocks whose mux shares its register with the gate and the
divider, that clears them. Merge in the current mux register contents
outside the mux field before the write.

Register the composite clocks with CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT, so that a
rate request changes the divider only and never switches the parent.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/clk/clk-k230.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/clk-k230.c b/drivers/clk/clk-k230.c
index 71d38f7d4..a9dd2c343 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/clk-k230.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-k230.c
@@ -499,6 +499,9 @@ static int k230_clk_composite_set_parent(struct clk_hw *hw, u8 index)
 				  << k230_composite->mux_shift;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(k230_composite->composite_spinlock, flags);
+	composite_mux_value |=
+		readl(k230_composite->mux_reg) &
+		~(k230_composite->mux_mask << k230_composite->mux_shift);
 	writel(composite_mux_value, k230_composite->mux_reg);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(k230_composite->composite_spinlock, flags);
 
@@ -765,7 +768,7 @@ static struct clk *_of_cannan_k230_clk_composite_setup(struct device_node *node)
 	init.parent_names = parent_name;
 	init.name = node->name;
 	init.ops = p_clk_ops;
-	init.flags = CLK_IS_BASIC /*|flags*/;
+	init.flags = CLK_IS_BASIC | CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT;
 	k230_clk_composite->hw.init = &init;
 
 	hw = &k230_clk_composite->hw;
